    "https://cityvisionuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/67kygv96KW/Adjunct-Faculty-In-Addiction-Counseling-At-Online-Christian-University": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Addiction Counseling at Online Christian University",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Addiction Counseling at Online Christian University - City Vision University - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Before you Apply Visit our Adjunct Faculty Page to review pay and expectations for adjunct faculty. Visit our Mission, Vision and Values page to assess whether there might be a fit. Adjunct Faculty in Addiction Counseling at Online Christian University Remote Contracted Mid Level Share This is a part-time, remote work-from-home adjunct faculty position including the following. This involves teaching or co-teaching eight week, online courses including the following Grading and providing feedback on student assignments Facilitating communication among students in online discussion boards including posting and grading student responses Participating in Zoom meetings with students (typically 2-3 meetings in total across 8 weeks) Completing City Vision University’s Faculty 101 onboarding course for new faculty. Required Qualifications Masters in a Counseling or Psychology-related field Must have strong attention to detail and organizational skills needed for accurate on-time grading Must be a US Citizen, permanent resident or have a valid work visa to work in the US Strongly Desired Qualifications Doctorate in a Counseling or Psychology-related field. Note: This is required for adjunct positions teaching graduate courses. Experience in addiction counseling and with clients from at-risk populations (strongly desired) Expected hours: typically requires about 1 hour per week per student across an 8 week course Compensation Faculty with Master's Degrees: $75 per student (guaranteed minimum of 6 students) Faculty with Doctoral Degrees: $125/student (guaranteed minimum of 6 students) See additional compensation details and expectations for this position here: https://www.cityvision.edu/online-adjunct-faculty-application/ About City Vision University City Vision University is an online-only, Christian institution with the goal of providing radically affordable education to those serving poor and addicted individuals. We currently offer Certificates, Bachelor's, Associate's and Master's in Nonprofit Management, Business and Ministry. Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Address Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file What's your citizenship / employment eligibility? * No answer I am a U.S. Citizen/Permanent Resident Non-citizen allowed to work for any employer Non-citizen allowed to work for current employer Non-citizen seeking work authorization I am a Canadian Citizen/Permanent Resident Other What's your highest level of education completed? * No answer GED or Equivalent High School Some College College - Associates College - Bachelor of Arts College - Bachelor of Fine Arts College - Bachelor of Science College - Master of Arts College - Master of Science College - Master of Fine Arts College - Master of Business Administration College - Doctorate Medical Doctor Other LinkedIn Profile URL: Do you meet ALL the following requirements? 1. Are you a Christian actively attending a church? 2. Are able to support City Vision's statement of faith? See: https://goo.gl/sqasUx 3. Do have a graduate degree in the subject area in which you desire to teach? Official transcript(s) required for all relevant degrees and/or licenses from an institution accredited by an accrediting agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education or accreditation in your home country recognized in the U.S. 4. Can you dedicate on the average of about 1 hour per week per student to facilitating students in the learning process? 5. Do you agree to support our mission as listed at: https://www.cityvision.edu/about/ ? * -- No answer -- Yes No Mission Alignment Please read our mission statement and history at http://www.cityvision.edu/about. Please describe how your passion and life calling aligns with our mission and focus on educating Christians that serve the poor and addicted? Are there aspects of your background that give you a particular passion for serving this audience? What experience do you have serving this audience? This typically is the most important question we consider in screening applications, so please take the time to answer this thoroughly. * Testimony/Spiritual Journey As a Christian University, the vibrancy of the faith and spiritual life of our faculty is important. Briefly share your testimony and spiritual journey. What church do you attend and what is your current church involvement? * Instruction Experience Please describe your experience in teaching. Do you have any experience in online teaching? Have you ever designed any online courses? * What courses are you able to teach? What is your subject matter expertise? What courses are you about to teach from this list: http://www.cityvision.edu/course-schedule (be sure to list full course name, not just the course number). If you have taught courses before please list the courses you have taught and whether they were online. * What online courses have you taught or designed? Please list any courses that you have either taught online or have written (if any). Only list accredited online courses. For each course, indicate whether you taught, designed it or did both. * Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
